{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1515906-as-above-so-bellow-a-new-spirit-world-based-on-the-human-mind","id":1515906,"title":"As Above, So Bellow - A New Spirit World Based on the Human Mind","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-06-22T16:28:26-07:00","id":1515906,"title":"As Above, So Bellow - A New Spirit World Based on the Human Mind","content":"<b>As Above, So Bellow.</b><br /> <br /> The mantra of real world hermeticism esoteric cults ever since the middle ages.<br /> <br /> So, thinking about that, I have had for a very, very long time, the idea of building the Spirit World based on the models of the human mind from psychology.<br /> <br /> I never actually had the time to put the effort into it... But I'll admit, I have been aided by ChatGPT in this effort.<br /> <br /> So, my basic idea was to have the &quot;Material Plane&quot; as a representarion of the &quot;Body&quot; (of &quot;God&quot;).<br /> <br /> The exterior world, that which exists outside of our minds, will be &quot;The Void&quot;. A &quot;realm&quot; of Qlippothic (&quot;anti-existance&quot;) energies that literally and metaphorically exists &quot;outside of God's boundaries&quot;.<br /> <br /> In this metaphor, The Void is the world outside of ourselves, outside of our minds.<br /> <br /> I have a list of realms I created with ChatGPT; our future Overlord helps me a big deal because he is much better at organising things than I am, my ideas are all over the place. The basic structure has been fluctuating as lose thoughts inside my brain for a few years now, and I already made a few changes, but they got lost in the mess of archives and consults with the ChatGPT archive.<br /> <br /> Before posting the many realms so far, I'll explain a bit of the basic structure: each realm is a combination of a &quot;common fantasy trope&quot; of spiritual places - things like &quot;heaven&quot; and &quot;hell&quot;, lands of the fairies, the underworld of the dead and such similar concepts.<br /> <br /> Thus, it's a &quot;mystic&quot; concept mixed with an aspect of the mind from Psychology.<br /> <br /> The basic structure with the cosmos will be BOTH triadic AND dualist... Yes. That's right. So, when you ask &quot;is the cosmos of your spirit world based on the concept of a triad, like in Hinduism, or dualist, like in Taoism?&quot;.<br /> <br /> And the answer to this question is... YES!<br /> <br /> Because it's BOTH.<br /> <br /> I'll explain: yes, we still have the good old &quot;Creation/Chaos, Order, Destruction&quot; from hinduism.<br /> <br /> However, that's NO LONGER the single aspect of my triad. <br /> <br /> Because... Now we have:<br /> Creation/Chaos - Id<br /> Order - Ego<br /> Destruction - Superego<br /> <br /> And, besides those, we also have:<br /> Struggle (between Id+Ego+Superego)<br /> Integration (between Id+Ego+Superego).<br /> <br /> Thus, Id (Chaos), Ego (Order) and Superego (Destruction) make the Triad system, but Struggle and Integration make the Dualist system.<br /> <br /> Besides Sttrugle and Integration, we also have another dual system in the psychological concepts of &quot;Pulse of Eros&quot; (Pulse of Life) and &quot;Pulse of Thanatos&quot; (Pulse of Death), forming a second layer of Dualism.<br /> <br /> So, Id, Ego, Superego, Struggle and Integration form the &quot;basic structure&quot; of the Spirit World. Yes, each has a realm of their own. For instance, &quot;Integration&quot; is the realm of &quot;Transcendence&quot;, and Struggle is &quot;The Abyss&quot;<br /> <br /> But it's more than that.<br /> <br /> This structure will repeat itself over EVERY single realm. Yes, this means that, for example, the Underworld will have a part relative to Chaos (Id), one relative to Order (Ego), one is Destruction (Superego), another will be Struggle and a final one being Integration.<br /> * In the specific case of the Underworld, the realm of the Restless Dead from the game &quot;Wraith the Oblivion&quot; would belong ONLY to the &quot;Struggle&quot; section of the Underworld. Integration would be the &quot;Elysian Fields&quot; or something like that, Im not sure yet.<br /> <br /> <b>As Above, so Bellow</b><br /> <br /> That's the main idea. Also, some realms would belong to the &quot;upper&quot; portion of &quot;Eros&quot; (life pulse) and &quot;Thanatos&quot; (death pulse). That structure will repeat itself over all realms.<br /> <br /> Now, the realms will be divided in ZONES. The first Zone is the &quot;Conscious Mind&quot;, represented by the &quot;Astral Plane&quot;.<br /> <br /> The first Realm anyone enters by leaving the Material World is the &quot;Mirrorworld&quot;. This realm represents the Self-Image as a concept of the mind. It is thus how an individual would see himself at a mirror, coloured by his own perceptions. Thus, Mirrorworld is a copy of the Material Plane... With a few distortions.<br /> <br /> The next realm is the &quot;Primal Wilds&quot; (Im still working on the name). This realm is a metaphor to the world of the SENSES. Thus, in here the spirit world still ressembles the Material Plane, and anyone can wander from Mirrorworld into Primal Wilds without even noticing.<br /> <br /> The third realm in this first Zone is the Astral Plane, which is also the first Zone itself. The Astral Plane is special, being accessible by Mind magics too.<br /> <br /> The Astral Plane streches over all other planes and zones, working as a membrane that separate each one of the different places of the spirit world.<br /> <br /> Trying to look inside a realm from the Astral Plane will only show you the &quot;reflective surface&quot;; this works like the superficiality of the conscious mind in relation to the depths of the subconscious. <br /> (also, without spirit magic is not possible to access those realms from the Astral Plane)<br /> <br /> Moving &quot;up&quot;, or &quot;outward&quot; (but I guess that it would be more accurate to say INWARDS), you get to the Subconscious Zone (I decided to call it &quot;Wonderland&quot;). In here you'll find realms like the Feywild and others.<br /> <br /> The last Zone is the &quot;Collective Unconscious&quot; holding several archetype realms &quot;like the Shadowlands&quot; (the Shadow) or the Anima/Animus, the Hero, the Self, the Persona, the Trickster, Wise King and Tyrant and Divine (Nurturer) Mother and the Dark Mother and others.<br /> <br /> Beyond that last layer is Nirvana, where the Ascended Ones are in a state of perfect Unity with the whole, and immediately above that (or intertwined with it) is Transcendence.<br /> <br /> Those last 2 realms however no longer are metaphors to the mind, but insted, to the SOUL (&quot;true self&quot;), with Transcendence basically being the &quot;Soul of The One&quot;.<br /> <br /> So, that's the initial blueprint of it all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-22T16:31:51-07:00","id":1515907,"title":"","content":"So, here's the first drawns of a few of the realms - I already have several changes in mind, let me just lay it all down here so I can organize that mess, otherwise it never leaves my head.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> **Greater Realms**<br /> <br /> 1. **Ethereal Plane**<br /> Link: Id<br /> Aspect: Realm of Creation/Chaos<br /> Purpose: Fostering the Manifestation of Infinite Possibilities and Chaotic Energies<br /> Ruler: Brahma &amp; The Holy Spirit (Hinduism/Christianity - Creator deity and aspect of the Holy Trinity) - Sustaining the creative forces and divine inspiration within the realm.<br /> <br /> 2. **Celestial Realm &amp; Elysian Fields**<br /> Link: Ego<br /> Aspect: Realm of Order<br /> Purpose: Sustaining Harmonious Balance, Divine Hierarchy, and Transcendent Beauty<br /> Ruler: Vishnu &amp; Jesus Christ (Hinduism/Christianity - Preserver deity and central figure of Christianity) - Ensuring the preservation of cosmic harmony and guiding souls towards divine perfection.<br /> <br /> 3. **Primal Forge**<br /> Link: Superego<br /> Aspect: Realm of Destruction and Renewal<br /> Purpose: Purging Imbalances, Transforming Old Patterns, and Catalyzing Renewal<br /> Ruler: Shiva &amp; God the Father (Hinduism/Christianity - Destroyer deity and the supreme God) - Overseeing the transformative processes and driving the renewal of energies within the realm.<br /> <br /> 4. **Transcendence**<br /> Link: Integration of the Self<br /> Aspect: Realm of Integration (Id, Ego, and Superego)<br /> Purpose: Unifying and Balancing the Triadic Forces of the Self for Spiritual Evolution<br /> Ruler: The One (Concept of divine unity) - Harmonizing the triadic forces and facilitating spiritual evolution and enlightenment.<br /> <br /> 5. **Abyss and Inferno**<br /> Link: Inner Struggles and Temptations<br /> Aspect: Realm of Demonic Entities and Unfathomable Darkness<br /> Purpose: Testing the Will, Overcoming Temptations, and Confronting Inner Demons<br /> Ruler: Shaitan/Ahriman (Islam/Zoroastrianism - Deity representing evil and darkness) - Challenging individuals to resist temptation and confront their inner demons.<br /> <br /> **Lesser Realms:**<br /> <br /> 6. **Underworld**<br /> Link: Memory<br /> Aspect: Realm of Departed Souls and Spirit Realms<br /> Purpose: Housing the Spirits of the Deceased, Preserving Ancestral Wisdom, and Governing the Cycle of Life and Death<br /> Ruler: Hades (Greek Mythology - God of the Underworld) - Governing the realm of the dead and preserving ancestral wisdom.<br /> <br /> 7. **Feywild**<br /> Link: Creativity<br /> Aspect: Realm of Enchanted Forests, Fae Folk, and Arcane Magic<br /> Purpose: Inspiring Boundless Creativity, Nurturing Imagination, and Facilitating Interactions with Fey Beings<br /> Ruler: Queen Mab (Shakespearean folklore - Queen of the Fairies) - Fostering creativity and maintaining the balance between humans and fey beings.<br /> <br /> 8. **Primal Wilds**<br /> Link: Sensorial World<br /> Aspect: Realm of Elemental Forces, Primal Energies, and Natural Harmony<br /> Purpose: Maintaining the Equilibrium of Nature, Nurturing Biodiversity, and Preserving the Balance of Elements<br /> Ruler: Gaia (Greek Mythology - Primordial deity of the Earth) - Sustaining the natural balance and fostering the harmony of elemental forces.<br /> <br /> 9. **Celestial Mountaintop**<br /> Link: Higher Self<br /> Aspect:<br /> <br /> Realm of Divine Wisdom and Illumination<br /> Purpose: Attaining Spiritual Enlightenment, Expanding Consciousness, and Gaining Transcendent Insight<br /> Ruler: Odin (Norse Mythology - Allfather and god of wisdom) - Guiding seekers towards spiritual enlightenment and bestowing divine wisdom.<br /> <br /> 10. **Dream World**<br /> Link: Dreams and Imagination<br /> Aspect: Realm of Lucid Dreams, Surreal Landscapes, and Infinite Possibilities<br /> Purpose: Exploring the Depths of Subconscious, Unleashing Creative Potential, and Unraveling the Mysteries of the Dream Realm<br /> Ruler: Morpheus (Greek Mythology - God of Dreams) - Governing the realm of dreams and unlocking the creative potential of the subconscious mind.<br /> <br /> 11. **Nirvana**<br /> Link: Peaceful Mind<br /> Aspect: Realm of Serenity, Bliss, and Transcendent Calm<br /> Purpose: Attaining Inner Peace, Liberation from Suffering, and Oneness with Universal Harmony<br /> Ruler: Buddha (Buddhism - Enlightened being and founder of Buddhism) - Guiding souls towards liberation from suffering and attaining inner peace.<br /> <br /> 12. **Astral Plane**<br /> Link: Consciousness<br /> Aspect: Realm of Expansive Consciousness and Cosmic Energies<br /> Purpose: Transcending Physical Limitations, Traveling through Astral Realms, and Exploring Multidimensional Awareness<br /> Ruler: Hermes Trismegistus (Hermeticism - Mythical figure representing wisdom and divine knowledge) - Navigating the astral realms and unlocking multidimensional awareness.<br /> <br /> 13. **Wonderland**<br /> Link: Subconscious<br /> Aspect: Realm of Mirrors, Illusions, and Subconscious Depths<br /> Purpose: Delving into the Abyss of Self-Reflection, Confronting Shadows, and Gaining Profound Insights into the Self<br /> Ruler: Dionysus (Greek Mythology - God of wine, ecstasy, and revelry) - Facilitating deep self-reflection and the exploration of subconscious depths.<br /> <br /> 14. **Shadowrealm**<br /> Link: Shadow Self<br /> Aspect: Realm of Dark Desires, Repressed Emotions, and Hidden Truths<br /> Purpose: Confronting and Integrating the Shadow Self, Unleashing Hidden Potential, and Embracing Wholeness<br /> Ruler: Lilith (Various mythologies - Mythical figure embodying darkness and female empowerment) - Guiding individuals to confront their shadow selves and embrace their hidden potential.<br /> <br /> 15. **Veiled Sanctum**<br /> Link: Intuition and Insight<br /> Aspect: Realm of Divine Knowledge, Prophetic Visions, and Esoteric Wisdom<br /> Purpose: Unlocking Intuitive Abilities, Receiving Divine Guidance, and Expanding Spiritual Perception<br /> Ruler: Apollo (Greek Mythology - God of prophecy, light, and knowledge) - Bestowing divine knowledge and facilitating intuitive abilities.<br /> <br /> 16. **Euphoria's Garden**<br /> Link: Emotions and Passions<br /> Aspect: Realm of Intense Emotions, Exquisite Pleasures, and Sensory Delights<br /> Purpose: Experiencing the Full Spectrum of Emotions, Finding Joy and Ecstasy, and Cultivating Emotional Awareness<br /> Ruler: Aphrodite (Greek Mythology - Goddess of love, beauty, and passion) - Inspiring and guiding the exploration of emotions and sensuality.<br /> <br /> 17. **The Labyrinth**<br /> Link: Fear and Anxiety<br /> Aspect: Realm of Endless Maze, Illusions, and Psychological Tests<br /> Purpose: Confronting and Overcoming Fears, Navigating Mental Challenges, and Gaining Inner Strength<br /> Ruler: <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28035,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","user":"Magus Maximus","date":". 06-22-2023, 07:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-22T16:35:14-07:00","id":1515909,"title":"","content":"Wouldn't a spirit world based on the mind be the High/Astral Umbra? Also, Chat GPT doesn't appear to know what purpose the WoD put the Qlippoth. Specifically, Mage, and even more specifically, as something practiced by Nephandi (Qlippothic Spheres). That might put a wrinkle in your world building.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-22T16:55:42-07:00","id":1515912,"title":"","content":"18. **Akashic Library**<br /> Link: Higher Consciousness<br /> Aspect: Realm of Cosmic Records, Universal Knowledge, and Collective Wisdom<br /> Purpose: Accessing Akashic Records, Gaining Insights into Past and Future, and Expanding Conscious Awareness<br /> Ruler: Thoth (Egyptian Mythology - God of knowledge, writing, and wisdom) - Preserving cosmic records and granting access to universal knowledge.<br /> <br /> 19. **Archetype's Nexus**<br /> Link: Collective Unconscious<br /> Aspect: Realm of Archetypes, Collective Symbols, and Collective Memory<br /> Purpose: Exploring Universal Archetypes, Understanding Deep Collective Patterns, and Connecting with the Unconscious Mind<br /> Ruler: Carl Jung (Psychology/Analytical Psychology - Swiss psychiatrist who explored the collective unconscious) - Unveiling archetypes and deep collective patterns within the realm.<br /> <br /> 20. **Mirrorworld**<br /> Link: Self Image<br /> Aspect: Spiritual reflection of the Material World and Gateway to other realms<br /> Purpose: Reflecting the Essence of the Material World, Facilitating Spiritual Reflection, and Serving as a Gateway to other Realms<br /> Ruler: Narcissus (Greek Mythology - Mythical figure reflecting self-obsession and introspection) - Revealing the true essence of the material world and enabling spiritual reflection.<br /> <br /> 21. **Sanctuary of Fortitude**<br /> Link: Inner Strength and Courage<br /> Aspect: Realm of Resilience, Inner Power, and Courageous Spirit<br /> Purpose: Cultivating Inner Strength, Overcoming Adversity, and Embodying Courage in the Face of Challenges<br /> Ruler: Athena (Greek Mythology - Goddess of wisdom, courage, and strategic warfare) - Nurturing inner strength and guiding individuals to overcome challenges with courage.<br /> <br /> 22. **Bridge of Unity**<br /> Link: Divine Love and Compassion<br /> Aspect: Realm of Divine Love, Unity, and Compassionate Action<br /> Purpose: Fostering Oneness, Healing Division, and Practicing Unconditional Love and Compassion<br /> Ruler: Quan Yin (Buddhism/Taoism - Bodhisattva of compassion and mercy) - Promoting divine love, unity, and compassionate actions within the realm.<br /> <br /> 23. **Citadel of Rationality**<br /> Link: Reason and Logic<br /> Aspect: Realm of Rational Thinking, Analytical Intellect, and Logical Discernment<br /> Purpose: Cultivating Clear Judgment, Objective Reasoning, and Developing Logical and Analytical Skills<br /> Ruler: Athena (Greek Mythology - Goddess of wisdom, strategic warfare, and rational thought) - Guiding logical reasoning, rationality, and analytical thinking within the realm.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-22T17:03:24-07:00","id":1515913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1515906-as-above-so-bellow-a-new-spirit-world-based-on-the-human-mind?p=1515912#post1515912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ruler: Quan Yin (Buddhism/Taoism - Bodhisattva of compassion and mercy) - Promoting divine love, unity, and compassionate actions within the realm.<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Quibble - in most Chinese and in particular Mandarin Romanization schemes, her name is written as Kuan Yin or Guanyin (an unaspirated k sound). Q as a k sound is more of a Vietnamese Romanization hallmark (In which case you would have Am instead of Yin); q in hanyu pinyin is used as a highly aspirated ch sound.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-22T17:16:26-07:00","id":1515914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1515906-as-above-so-bellow-a-new-spirit-world-based-on-the-human-mind?p=1515909#post1515909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wouldn't a spirit world based on the mind be the High/Astral Umbra? Also, Chat GPT doesn't appear to know what purpose the WoD put the Qlippoth. Specifically, Mage, and even more specifically, as something practiced by Nephandi (Qlippothic Spheres). That might put a wrinkle in your world building.</div> </div> </div> </div>ChatGPT is not the brain behind this operation, I am. In fact, that dumb thing makes me wanna punch my magic pocket mirror with all its dumb mistakes (but I do hope it finds the magnificency to forgive an insect like me once it fully awakens as the God-machine for insulting it).<br /> <br /> Also, the meaning ChatGPT uses for the Qliphoth is the Jewish/Kabbalist meaning (something like &quot;malformed pieces of the Creation rejected by God&quot;), which actually serves well enough both for WoD, but even better, it serves my own purposes even better.<br /> <br /> Since the &quot;cosmos&quot; in this system will be &quot;God&quot; (or &quot;The One&quot;) [the &quot;Tellurian for WoD], then the jewish kabbalist meaning of it is perfect for my analogy of the &quot;Deep Umbra&quot; equivalent being the Outside World - AKA, that which is outside of our minds.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1515906-as-above-so-bellow-a-new-spirit-world-based-on-the-human-mind?p=1515909#post1515909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wouldn't a spirit world based on the mind be the High/Astral Umbra</div> </div> </div> </div>No. That's not it at all. The High/Astral Umbra is just... A mess.<br /> <br /> This idea of &quot;spirit world&quot; based on the mind is just structuring the spirit worlds in a way similar to how the human mind works; it has nothing to do with finding the abstract concept of &quot;Lord Ketch, the spirit King of Ketchup&quot; from some weird abstract realm in the astral clouds.<br /> <br /> What that means is that, for example, the &quot;Feywild&quot; (or &quot;The Dreaming&quot; if you will) is a realm inside the &quot;Wonderland&quot; (Subconscious) Zone.<br /> <br /> This means that the &quot;Underworld&quot; (Memory) is no longer in the &quot;Low Umbra&quot; (because there is no such &quot;Zone&quot;), but rather is MOSTLY inside the Subconscious Zone (a piece of it will also be inside the Conscious Zone).<br /> <br /> That's why the Astral Plane, as a metaphor for the Conscious Mind in my model, stretches from &quot;Mirrorworld&quot; and &quot;Primal Wilds&quot; (Self Image and World of Senses) over all other Realms and Zones, but it only shows a reflection of those realms - much like the Conscious Mind is just a tiny layer on top of the Subconscious.<br /> <br /> It's a metaphorical analogy. Saying it is &quot;modeled in the human mind&quot; has nothing to do with it being &quot;realms of thought&quot; (althought they sort of are, but in truth, those are all worlds of &quot;ephemera&quot;, worlds of spirit)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-22T17:50:39-07:00","id":1515917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1515906-as-above-so-bellow-a-new-spirit-world-based-on-the-human-mind?p=1515913#post1515913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Quibble - in most Chinese and in particular Mandarin Romanization schemes, her name is written as Kuan Yin or Guanyin (an unaspirated k sound). Q as a k sound is more of a Vietnamese Romanization hallmark (In which case you would have Am instead of Yin); q in hanyu pinyin is used as a highly aspirated ch sound.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bah, ChatGPT make some weird choices. I dont know who that is. I'll favor rulers from Roman/Greek, Egyptian, Norse mythologies, some Hindu, some Aztec, Christian, Jewish, Mesopotamic. I only know 2 chinese gods (Guan Yu and Sun Wukong). I wont be apologetic about it. I picked rulers that picked my interest, using mythological Gods. But some choices were made by ChatGPT resulting in... That. I'll take what Im familiar with, but I accept suggestions.<br /> <br /> There are several modifications I wanna make. First of all, after some research Im leaning towards dividing The Abyss into 6 realms (urgh, that pains me). This will be based into all kinds of conflicts:<br /> <br /> 1. Struggle (Id+Ego): Inner Conflict of Desires<br /> Consequences: Impulsivity, Guilty and Anxiety, Lack of Balance<br /> <br /> 2. Struggle (Id+Superego): Battle of Instincts and Morality<br /> Consequences: Moral Dilemmas, Internal Conflict (Guilty or Shame), Repression or Rebellion<br /> <br /> 3. Struggle (Ego+Superego): Conflict of Self and Society<br /> Consequences: Identity Crisis, Anxiety and Frustration, Self-Reflection and Growth<br /> <br /> So, initially I thought about &quot;Gehenna&quot; as the realm for the Struggle of Id+Ego, &quot;Inferno&quot; for Id+Superego and &quot;Niflheim&quot; for Ego+Superego.<br /> <br /> Each would &quot;attract&quot; different types of sinners: for example, the nazis that commited atrocities for pleasure, would go to inferno, while the ones that were &quot;just&quot; &quot;following orders&quot; would go to Niflheim.<br /> <br /> Gehenna would be a hell for hedonists, Inferno a hell for amoral people and Niflheim a hell for &quot;self betrayal&quot; or &quot;crimes against self&quot; (like betraying your own consciousness due to social pressure or the ultimate crime against self - suicide).<br /> <br /> But then, I searched more and... Each of this conflicts could have one aspect overcoming the other, so it's actually 6 possible divisions:<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>&quot;ChatGPT</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here is a concise list of the stances where one aspect overcomes another,<br /> along with a brief description of the struggles and consequences associated<br /> with each:<br /> <br /> 1. Id Overcoming Ego:<br /> Struggle: Inner conflict between primal desires and rationality.<br /> Consequences: Impulsive behavior, lack of self-control, disregard for consequences.<br /> <br /> 2. Ego Overcoming Id:<br /> Struggle: Balancing personal desires with societal norms and values.<br /> Consequences: Repression of instinctual desires, adherence to social expectations, conformity.<br /> <br /> 3. Id Overcoming Superego:<br /> Struggle: Conflict between primal desires and moral conscience.<br /> Consequences: Moral transgressions, guilt, self-indulgence, disregard for societal norms.<br /> <br /> 4. Superego Overcoming Id:<br /> Struggle: Internal battle between moral conscience and instinctual desires.<br /> Consequences: Suppression of desires, self-restraint,<br /> feelings of guilt and self-criticism.<br /> <br /> 5. Ego Overcoming Superego:<br /> Struggle: Balancing personal desires and individuality with moral standards.<br /> Consequences: Striving for personal fulfillment, navigating moral dilemmas, self-reflection.<br /> <br /> 6. Superego Overcoming Ego:<br /> Struggle: Overemphasis on moral standards and<br /> self-criticism.<br /> Consequences: Excessive guilt, self-repression, self-denial, diminished sense of personal identity.</div> </div> </div> </div>So now Im back at square 1.\u200b<br /> Good thing is, I can divide all of those between &quot;Excessive pulse of Life&quot; and &quot;Excessive pulse of Death.<br /> Basically, &quot;hells&quot; 1, 3 and 5 are &quot;excessive life&quot; driven and &quot;hells&quot; 2, 4 and 6 are &quot;excessive death&quot; driven. I just need to find examples fitting with these themes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-23T01:24:43-07:00","id":1515933,"title":"","content":"I can see where you are going with this, but as a recommendation I would treat it as a model of a specific paradigm (hermeticism) rather than a definitive structure. Nothing wrong with that, just keep in mind that the Umbrae or spiritual realms have to cover and stay compatible with <i>many</i> different views, doubly so if you're using it cross-splat. Even within the hermetic traditions there are different ideas on how to model this- on the upside, nothing prevents a character with a particular paradigm to experience the Umbrae through their vision of how things work.<br /> <br /> You may want to have a look at the <a href=\"https://archive.org/details/kybalionstudyofh00init/page/112/mode/2up\" target=\"_blank\">Kybalion</a> for a more Jungian model of the planes within the hermetic context. Not to replace your Freudian model, but it could be used to amend it (and provides an example of how the same tradition with the same paradigm can have different interpretations).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-23T04:02:36-07:00","id":1515939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1515906-as-above-so-bellow-a-new-spirit-world-based-on-the-human-mind?p=1515933#post1515933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can see where you are going with this, but as a recommendation I would treat it as a model of a specific paradigm (hermeticism) rather than a definitive structure. Nothing wrong with that, just keep in mind that the Umbrae or spiritual realms have to cover and stay compatible with <i>many</i> different views, doubly so if you're using it cross-splat. Even within the hermetic traditions there are different ideas on how to model this- on the upside, nothing prevents a character with a particular paradigm to experience the Umbrae through their vision of how things work.<br /> <br /> You may want to have a look at the <a href=\"https://archive.org/details/kybalionstudyofh00init/page/112/mode/2up\" target=\"_blank\">Kybalion</a> for a more Jungian model of the planes within the hermetic context. Not to replace your Freudian model, but it could be used to amend it (and provides an example of how the same tradition with the same paradigm can have different interpretations).</div> </div> </div> </div>Problem is that the Umbra already is like this. More or less.<br /> <br /> Im not trying to imprint hermeticism/gnosticism into it, in fact Im not even devising this for playing WoD specifically (Im worldbuilding for a fantasy world of the D&amp;D likeness, medieval fantasy trope).<br /> <br /> I liked the whole mantra of &quot;as above, so bellow&quot; just for a general &quot;artistic concept&quot; for it all.<br /> <br /> What's also important to note is that the WoD already follows generally a gnostic/hermetic/theosophical view. You may notice that the WoD's &quot;Umbra&quot; has the Low, Mid and High Umbras, which more or less ressembles the 3 Zones (consciousness, subconscious, collective unconscious) that I described. You can also notice how the Fae come from the Dreaming and that, despite not made it explicitly like I did, the world of the Wraith the Oblivion is a world of memories.<br /> <br /> The spirit world of WoD is not composed of Heaven, Hell and Purgatory, which would be the Christian view; it's not the 6 states of existance from Buddhism, nor is it the jewish Sheol or the pagans Hades, Elysian Fields, Tartarus and Olympus, or the 9 realms connected by Yggdrasil (the tree of life).<br /> <br /> The WoD cosmology is specifically hermeticist/theosophical - the idea that all religions are actually just one, the hermetic concept of the theological &quot;truth&quot; being like a diamond, and each different religion is just a facet of it.<br /> <br /> To begin with, WoD is Animist and Totemist, the old pagan idea that everything has an spirit and has spirit representation; that already goes against most of 99% of modern religions.<br /> <br /> So no, you can NOT have a Spirit World that embraces &quot;different paradigms&quot;. The writers says that it does, but that's just simply not true. The WoD cosmology is entirely Theosophical in its nature.<br /> <br /> Now, I wasnt trying to imprint Theosophy/Hermeticism on my model, and the reason why it resulted in something similar to the WoD model is entirely coincidental. I would say that the WoD already tried to use those elements of the psyche, but as I always say, while the writers of WoD abound in creativity, they lack in organization and methodical planning. Too much glamour not tempered by a healthy dose of banality.<br /> <br /> Also, the &quot;spirit worlds&quot; from real world mythologies already are filled with psychological aspects. That is nothing new to me, since they were all invented by humans after all. So for example, the 6 states of existance in Buddhism are based on psychological aspects. The Christian Hell punishes several sins (Glutony, Lust, Avarice, etc etc).<br /> <br /> All those ancient people's knew in a subjective way many of the modern concepts of psychology. Hell, the very name of the science comes from the greek Goddess &quot;Psyche&quot;, the Goddess of the Mind. Several concepts of psychology are described as greek Gods - Eros/Thanatos (&quot;pulse of life&quot; vs &quot;pulse of death&quot;), Narcisism/Eco (from the story of Narciso and the Nymph Eco) and several others.<br /> <br /> The ancient people had an intuitive wisdom about all these concepts that would end up forming their religions. So, it makes sense to just formalize it all with the more theoretical and formalized structure of the good ol' doctors Freud and Jung, rather than just subjective and intuitive like the ancients.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-23T05:05:09-07:00","id":1515940,"title":"","content":"I wasn't arguing your ideas, just pointing out that whatever model you choose, it is by necessity going to be looking through one of those facets of the diamond - so it shouldn't be handled as definitive, but a point of view <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I also apologize for assuming that your structure was intentionally hermetic, but that may happen when your lead in is one of the core hermetic principles. I was trying to help by providing material for developing the idea, but that was based on a false assumption.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-23T14:50:22-07:00","id":1515964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1515906-as-above-so-bellow-a-new-spirit-world-based-on-the-human-mind?p=1515940#post1515940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wasn't arguing your ideas, just pointing out that whatever model you choose, it is by necessity going to be looking through one of those facets of the diamond - so it shouldn't be handled as definitive, but a point of view <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Of course, but there is a need for an objective point of view, otherwise the &quot;Spirit World&quot; would just become a solipsistic illusory world, tailored for each one venturing there. Now, whatever vision shared for it, be it the egyptian Duat or the 9 realms connected by Yggdrasil or the heaven governed by the Celestial Bureocracy, unless again it is a solipsistic world upon which everybody sees what they think they should see, in which case it would be an absolutely individual experience and only cultural background/religious/ideological beliefs would make that experience close enough for certain groups to share some similar (but NEVER identical) views, but except in this case, one vision MUST, be definition, be the objective truth, and the others are just simply wrong.<br /> <br /> Like I said, WoD suffers from the same &quot;sin&quot;. Because the truth is that the WoD Umbra is absolutely Theosophical/Hermetic in nature. To begin with, it is an Animist/Totemist world, which already contradicts 90% of all religious faiths of the world today. And there's no point of view in here: in the WoD, I could be an atheist materialist technocrat, and that wont change the fact that the rocks have spirits of their own. In that case, I would just simply be wrong.<br /> <br /> Granted, the confusion is of my own fault. When I said &quot;As above, so bellow&quot;, I clearly evoked visions of medieval hermeticist wizards speaking nonsense inside of their &quot;wizard circles&quot;.<br /> <br /> I just wanted to throw some little bits of &quot;esoteric fairy dust&quot; over it all. The main concept instead is how Id, Ego and Superego (or even in other words: Chaos/Creation, Order, Destruction) are the main principles of the human psyche, and how those interplay every aspects of our psyches. Which is why they repeat in the realm of Memory (Underworld), Dreams (Feywild) and every other.<br /> <br /> The fact that this makes hermeticism be somewhat &quot;the right stuff&quot; was purely coincidental. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I also apologize for assuming that your structure was intentionally hermetic, but that may happen when your lead in is one of the core hermetic principles. I was trying to help by providing material for developing the idea, but that was based on a false assumption. </div> </div> </div>The problem is that real life hermeticism likes to keep adding facets to the diamont. It's not a real religion, but rather a syncretic cult of &quot;pick and chose&quot; flavor of the moment esoteric thing.<br /> <br /> For this reason, ANYTHING can be hermeticism. But that wasnt the angle I was aiming at.<br /> <br /> However, in the context of the world, it isnt absolutely clear the connection. I mean, since I am the Alpha and Omega of this world, I know that &quot;Wonderland&quot; (or whatever better name I can conjure) means the Subconscious, but that doesnt mean that the mystics of said world are capable of making that connection.<br /> <br /> To the wizards astrally travelling around it all sounds like some crazy acid trip, rather than a class with Sigmund Freud and Carl Jung.<br /> <br /> For this reason too, the hermetics are NOT right. Not in this world. No group is. Because anyone travelling these worlds will inevitably mistake the parts for the whole. Which is why different groups end up with vastly different conclusions.<br /> <br /> In truth, this structure is for the eyes of Gods only - this absolute knowledge is for the Storyteller only. My players can come up with any ideas that they'd like, they'll never see the above notes.<br /> <br /> So, rather than a world based on hermeticism, it's a world based on psychology, sprinkled with some fairy dust (after all, calling &quot;hell&quot; as &quot; Realm of Struggle between Id+Ego+Superego&quot; would not only make it obvious, but also boring as hell).<br /> <br /> But any ideas on &quot;generic mysticism&quot; are more than welcome for me to add - after all, the idea is to use psychology with a bit of mysticism in it.<br /> <br /> And there's no need to apologize, quite the opposite, I appreciate the help","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-25T10:08:19-07:00","id":1516108,"title":"","content":"Some of these ideas are ever so slightly similar to some I've posted about the Umbra in various posts, most recently in Mage based on the &quot;triple axis&quot; theory, where there are six major realms surrounding a seventh. Three of the major realms are aligned to one of the Triatic forces of Werewolf/Mage balanced by an opposite realm where the other to forces are supposed to be in balance, although they aren't always. My extrapolation has each realm subdivided into five levels, although not all levels are equal nor are they currently fully expressed. The central seventh realm is the whole that each of the other reflects. Yes, the physical realm would be one of the six and not the central hub. Some of your thoughts mirror some of the work I have done, although my work is more closely tied to the actual cosmologies expressed in the WOD as opposed to the 'real world' philosophical and mystical teachings as yours are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>THWarted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17984-toby-weingarten","name":"Toby Weingarten","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-25T20:39:48-07:00","id":1516169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Toby Weingarten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1515906-as-above-so-bellow-a-new-spirit-world-based-on-the-human-mind?p=1516108#post1516108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some of these ideas are ever so slightly similar to some I've posted about the Umbra in various posts, most recently in Mage based on the &quot;triple axis&quot; theory, where there are six major realms surrounding a seventh. Three of the major realms are aligned to one of the Triatic forces of Werewolf/Mage balanced by an opposite realm where the other to forces are supposed to be in balance, although they aren't always. My extrapolation has each realm subdivided into five levels, although not all levels are equal nor are they currently fully expressed. The central seventh realm is the whole that each of the other reflects. Yes, the physical realm would be one of the six and not the central hub. Some of your thoughts mirror some of the work I have done, although my work is more closely tied to the actual cosmologies expressed in the WOD as opposed to the 'real world' philosophical and mystical teachings as yours are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it is a &quot;non-coincidental coincidence&quot;. Most mystic traditions take into consideration SOME aspects of the human mind and/or the natural world - after all, they were created by humans (but of course that's easy for a skeptical atheist materialist like me to say).<br /> <br /> The WoD Umbra is filled with many many things similar to my ideas - which is a coincidence born out of that fact, but also because all that structure is in some way inside of our subconscious. I was bringing it intentionally based on the scientific literature about that, but I have no doubt that when writting the Umbra, the writers let their subconscious creativity work them in that direction - as did you too, by the way.<br /> <br /> I also liked the whole &quot;7 realms&quot; because it ties to the numerology of the &quot;divine number&quot; being 7... Just some hippidity hoppity ocus pocus pointy hat nerdy stuff to add a little &quot;ooh, look at all my mysticism in action&quot; to the mix.<br /> <br /> I also did some pretty awesome images of the &quot;Divine Symbol of the Universe&quot;... If I can just learn how to upload those...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-25T20:50:13-07:00","id":1516170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><figure class=\"image bbcode-attachment align_center\"><img alt=\"Chaos/Creation, Order, Destruction, 3 Struggles, Integration\" title=\"7 Realms\" data-align=\"center\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://postimg.cc/9wpBTPqN\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://postimg.cc/9wpBTPqN\" data-thumb-url=\"https://postimg.cc/9wpBTPqN\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"Caption\" class=\"bbcode-attachment js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><figcaption>Caption</figcaption></figure></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://postimg.cc/0bqfkWdp\" target=\"_blank\">https://postimg.cc/0bqfkWdp<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://postimages.org/\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://i.postimg.cc/rFDY97DY/21275834.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a></a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28035,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","user":"Magus Maximus","date":". 06-26-2023, 12:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-25T20:53:43-07:00","id":1516173,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://postimg.cc/9wpBTPqN\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://i.postimg.cc/vDR2J38M/29002894.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://postimg.cc/9wpBTPqN\" target=\"_blank\"> 29002894 &mdash; Postimages </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://postimg.cc/9wpBTPqN\" target=\"_blank\"> https://postimg.cc/9wpBTPqN </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Lets see if this works<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://postimages.org/\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://i.postimg.cc/vDR2J38M/29002894.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a><br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28035,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","user":"Magus Maximus","date":". 06-26-2023, 12:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-25T21:19:54-07:00","id":1516178,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://postimages.org/\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://i.postimg.cc/zXqTzhrw/99868698.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-25T21:26:05-07:00","id":1516179,"title":"","content":"That would be the &quot;basic layout&quot; for the &quot;Divine Symbol&quot;. I thought about some dozen combinations involving triangles and circles and squares lol<br /> <br /> The simplified and more &quot;abstract symbol&quot; rather than an artistic view would be as follows, with each red circle being Chaos/Creation (Id), Order (Ego) and Destruction (Superego) respectively, the 3 intersections between each 2 circles being an &quot;perfect imperfect&quot; (for being out of place individually, but the 3 together are actually symmetrically aligned) &quot;struggle&quot;, and the intersection between the 3 is Integration. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://postimages.org/\" target=\"_blank\"><img data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.postimg.cc/G36hzwM4/images.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.postimg.cc/G36hzwM4/images.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.postimg.cc/G36hzwM4/images.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/></a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28035,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","user":"Magus Maximus","date":". 06-26-2023, 12:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-26T16:52:56-07:00","id":1516282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wikipedia</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The <b>autonomic nervous system</b> (<b>ANS</b>), formerly referred to as the <b>vegetative nervous system</b>, is a division of the <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nervous_system\" target=\"_blank\">nervous system</a> that supplies <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Viscera\" target=\"_blank\">internal organs</a>, smooth muscle and glands.<sup><a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Autonomic_nervous_system#cite_note-Dorlands-1\" target=\"_blank\">[1]</a></sup> The autonomic nervous system is a control system that acts largely unconsciously and regulates bodily functions, such as the <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heart_rate\" target=\"_blank\">heart rate</a>, its force of contraction, <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Digestion\" target=\"_blank\">digestion</a>, <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Respiratory_rate\" target=\"_blank\">respiratory rate</a>, <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pupillary_dilation\" target=\"_blank\">pupillary response</a>, <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Micturition\" target=\"_blank\">urination</a>, and <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sexual_arousal\" target=\"_blank\">sexual arousal</a>.<sup><a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Autonomic_nervous_system#cite_note-Human_Physiology_-_Janig-2\" target=\"_blank\">[2]</a></sup> This system is the primary mechanism in control of the <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fight-or-flight_response\" target=\"_blank\">fight-or-flight response</a>.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course! I got myself so caught up on the psychological aspects of our consciousness and what makes us human that I forgot about our &quot;worm-brains&quot;! I forgot all those pieces of our &quot;minds&quot; that dont get Freudian-Jungian at all, but rather the parts the regulate all of the revulsive inside of our meatbags packages!<br /> <br /> Ok, so new plan: the &quot;Primal Wilds&quot; (I still need a better plan) will no longer represent the world of the Senses, but rather it will be all those parts of our nervous system that dont go into the &quot;soul&quot; of us, but rather keep our bodily functions independent of our childhood repressed sexual desires for our mothers/fathers. It's going to be the part of the Spirit World responsible for keeping the Material Plane &quot;Pulsating&quot;. As such, this is the one area that is NOT accessible via Astral Plane AT ALL. There will be some connections towards Realms of Emotions and Realms of Senses, but that's about it. Transitioning between the &quot;Psychological Umbra&quot; and the &quot;Physiological Umbra&quot; will be hard and use hard to find pathways.<br /> <br /> Thus, this &quot;Physiological Umbra&quot; would be more akin to the &quot;Gaia World&quot; of the Werebeasts from WoD.<br /> <br /> Another idea I had was to make all Spirit Worlds have &quot;Rainbow Bridges&quot;, which are the pathways connecting different realms and/or zones.<br /> <br /> Those &quot;Rainbow Bridges&quot; will confer an eternal Aurora visage on ALL spiritual skies, increasing the sense of wonder of alien-like nature of these worlds, and those will represent the synapses and the interactions between thoughts - for example, a Rainbow Bridge opening between the Astral Plane and the Underworld would represent a memory being remembered and coming to the conscious mind, while a Rainbow Bridge between the Feywild and Astral Plane would represent the conscious mind creating imagined fantasy scenarios/ideas, and a &quot;Dark Bridge&quot; between the Abyss and the Underworld could represent a dark memory being repressed in the confines of the subconscious mind for example.<br /> <br /> Spirits of each realm in this sense could literally be seem as &quot;God's thoughts&quot;. Demons escaping the Abyss would be like repressed Dark Thoughts trying to rage and escape from their cage (just as Freud described, repressed thoughts come back with a vengeance).<br /> <br /> So guys, please give some suggestions, ideas, imputs, criticism... Did anyone like it, hate it or what","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}